      "text": "First, let's determine the smallest positive angle that is congruent to $\\frac{11 \\pi}{3}$:\n$$\\frac{11 \\pi}{3} - 2\\pi = \\frac{11 \\pi}{3} - \\frac{6 \\pi}{3} = \\frac{5 \\pi}{3}.$$\nTherefore, $\\sin \\frac{11 \\pi}{3} = \\sin \\frac{5 \\pi}{3}.$\nThe angle $\\frac{5 \\pi}{3}$ is found in the unit circle as:\n$$\\frac{5 \\pi}{3} = 2\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{3}.$$\nThis means $\\frac{5 \\pi}{3}$ is 2 full rotations plus an additional $\\frac{\\pi}{3}.$\nSince sine is periodic with a period of $2 \\pi$ and negative angles indicate the distance is measured in the opposite direction on the unit circle, we have:\n$$\\sin \\frac{5 \\pi}{3} = -\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{3}.$$\nFinally, we know that the sine of the $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$ angle is $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$.\nTherefore, $\\sin \\frac{5 \\pi}{3} = \\boxed{-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}.$",
